  "note": "Hand-verified callers/callees of stable methods in src/flask/app.py, read directly from source (not echoed from the graph). Scope = INTRA-REPO call targets only: calls into external deps (werkzeug, blinker signals, logging) have no graph node and are excluded, so a missing edge reflects a real resolution gap, not an out-of-corpus call. Peer keys are <dotted-package-path>.<qualified-name> (Python package paths carry no '/', so trace.peerKey keeps the full dotted path). The wsgi_app probe is the cross-language signal: the current tree-sitter extractor captures self.method() calls but drops ctx.push()/ctx.pop() (instance dispatch on a typed local) — exactly what go/types resolves and #468 aims to recover. Scored via: dex bench trace run --project <flask> --gold benchmark/trace/flask-py.json",
